    "_note": "OUTDOORS3 / DUNGON3 (the same drawing lines, v1.0 and v3.0) 1540-2006, 4000-4160, 9100-9220 (GRAPHICS.md section 9): the round plays on the game's one hi-res screen (SCREEN, the index's screens.frame): the field box bottom right, the message box (650: columns 17-38, rows 9-11) above it, the party columns (600-635) on top; the options and orders (1068-1470) are the remaster's screen. monster_plot: MONSTER PLOT sprites (whole bytes) with their top-left at byte column 21 + 4 * INT(5 * (i + .5) / n) (1550), the front rank (the larger group, 1047) at y 120 (99 for S% 21, a giant), the second at 96 (1540); pose B from a swing, spell or breath to the round's end (2006); blanked at the death (4145). Party slot k at (147 + 19k, 198 - 8 * (row + 1)) (9100: back 190, middle 182, front 174): a FIRE order draws shape 2 for the figure, 3 once it shot (9200, 1624); a hurt leg kneels (shape 6 + the arm); else the body (TOWN3 2350-2360, social class 3: shape 4 but over 25) with arm 20, 22 from a swing (1695), 5 from a cast (1760), 21 for a parry that took (1527 / 9210); a member's death erases the figure (4025). The sparkle (23) at the figure's point + (14, -23) during the cast tones (1762-1764); 4132 XDRAWs shape 47 - 23 * SP at (7 * X% + 3, Y% + 20) for 500 loops: the spell hit (24, SP = 1) or the arrow of a bow hit (1, SP = 2); a bow miss (1628) the arrow at (220, 104), (220, 105) in DUNGON3, for 250 loops, then the PA pause. Pauses: PA = 120 * TIME LAG loops a line (STARTER 361, 7560); loop_ms a rule of thumb for an empty Applesoft FOR / NEXT pass [~]; sparkle_ms the cast tones' length (CALL 770 not timed) [?]. The elemental (slot 6: its byte 168 is not known [?]) is not drawn.",
